(PRC-49 — a reap of a PID that is not your child sets the error flag and
 `On error` catches it (ECHILD).
 Also covers: PRC-47 (the reap returns a negative value on error — -10 is
 -ECHILD).
 999999 is a deliberately invalid PID, not somebody else's process: reaping
 can only ever touch your own children, so nothing outside this program is
 reachable here.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-49.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the foreign reap set the error flag
   it returned -10
)
a number called 'the foreign reap' is reap process 999999.
On error print "the foreign reap set the error flag".
print "it returned {'the foreign reap'}".
